# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Derived data. Everything under records/ is rebuilt from the dispatcher's run
# directories by tools/record_index.py, analysis/index_tables.R and tools/grade.py.
# None of it is evidence: the evidence lives in $DSH_HOME/harness-dispatcher/runs,
# which this repo only reads.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
records/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Rendered reports. The source of truth is REPORT.qmd; the HTML is what Quarto
# writes out of it, all at once, on every render. Tracking it means every edit to
# the source produces a diff of a hundred thousand lines that nobody can review,
# and it comes back as CRLF each time while the source stays LF. Render it locally:
# it embeds its own figures, so it opens offline and needs no CDN.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.html

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Workspaces, if a slot root is ever pointed inside the repo.
# A slot holds what the subject wrote — that is observation, and it belongs next to
# the run that produced it, not in a commit. Keeping the default outside the repo is
# the real protection; this line is for the day someone overrides $ASSAY_SLOTS.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
slots/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Python
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# R
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.Rhistory
.Rapp.history
.RData
.Rproj.user/
# A plot drawn without an explicit device lands in the working directory by default.
Rplots.pdf
renv/library/
renv/local/
renv/cellar/
renv/sandbox/
renv/staging/
renv/python/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local state and residue
# .bak-assay is what tools/patch_host_notice.py writes beside the host package, so it
# should never appear here — but a stray editor or patch backup in the repo is noise.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.log
*.tmp
*.bak
*.bak-*
*.orig
*.rej
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Editors and OS
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*~
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store
